Public-release gate: ivms101 2.0.0

The installed `ivms101@2.0.0` package metadata, npm registry metadata, and
published tarball do not provide a conclusive license field, repository URL,
homepage, or included LICENSE file. Its README states MIT and refers to a
LICENSE file that is absent from the package. Bundled IVMS specification text
also declares separate Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivatives 4.0 terms.

This evidence is internally inconsistent and is not sufficient to conclude
that every shipped file or the package as a whole may be redistributed under
MIT. The issue is unresolved. Keep the Defy repository private and do not
publish a release or container distribution until authoritative upstream
license evidence and the treatment of bundled specification material are
reviewed and documented.
